###
# RunPod Rust Service - HTTP Examples
# Use with REST Client extension in VS Code
# Or copy/paste curl commands into terminal
###

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@endpointId = your-endpoint-id-here

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. RunPod API Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-health

### 3. Execute Endpoint (Synchronous)
POST {{baseUrl}}/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endpoint_id": "{{endpointId}}",
  "input": {
    "prompt": "Hello from Rust service!",
    "temperature": 0.7
  },
  "sync": true,
  "timeout": 30000
}

### 4. Execute Endpoint (Asynchronous)
POST {{baseUrl}}/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "endpoint_id": "{{endpointId}}",
  "input": {
    "prompt": "This is an async job",
    "max_tokens": 100
  },
  "sync": false,
  "timeout": 30000
}

### 5. Get Job Status
# Replace 'job-123' with actual job ID from async execution
GET {{baseUrl}}/status/{{endpointId}}/job-123

### 6. Cancel Job
# Replace 'job-123' with actual job ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/cancel/{{endpointId}}/job-123

### 7. Poll Job Until Complete
# Replace 'job-123' with actual job ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/poll/{{endpointId}}/job-123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "max_wait_time": 300000,
  "poll_interval": 2000
}

### 8. Poll with Default Settings
POST {{baseUrl}}/poll/{{endpointId}}/job-123
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###
# Curl Command Examples
###

# Health Check
# curl http://localhost:3001/health

# Execute Sync
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/execute \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"endpoint_id":"your-endpoint-id","input":{"prompt":"test"},"sync":true,"timeout":30000}'

# Get Status
# curl http://localhost:3001/status/your-endpoint-id/job-123

# Cancel Job
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/cancel/your-endpoint-id/job-123

# Poll Job
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/poll/your-endpoint-id/job-123 \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"max_wait_time":300000,"poll_interval":2000}'
